0,"stage":"real task","check":{"n":200,"landed":0.0,"offpad":0.0,"timeout":0.0,"boulder":0.2,"crashed":0.8,"score":-529.1416110282328},"champion":"runs/bake_A_ppo_scratch/champions/i00000_s0_goal.json","run":"bake_A_ppo_scratch","replay":"replays/bake_A_ppo_scratch_0002.gif"},{"t":"2026-10-30 19:15:04","kind":"run_start","it":0,"steps":0,"stage_index":0,"note":"Bake-off candidate A: PPO from scratch (random 2x128 network) on the real task only. Reward: game score + 200 for resting between the flags, -100 off-pad rest, -100 timeout.","run":"bake_A_ppo_scratch"},{"t":"2026-10-30 19:15:04","kind":"stage_start","it":0,"steps":0,"stage_index":0,"stage":"real task","expect":"Learns to fly and land within ~10-20M steps; unlikely to beat the 84% pilot within 45 minutes.","run":"bake_A_ppo_scratch"},{"t":"2026-10-30 19:12:18","title":"Day 1: the machine, the frozen task and the baselines","text":"Machine: Intel i5-8250U, 4 cores / 8 threads, 7.6 GB RAM, no usable GPU (Intel UHD 620), so everything runs on the CPU. The task code (env.py, route_params.json and teacher.py, which env.py's route sensors use) is copied unchanged from the NEAT project and sha256-tested. 14 tests pass: determinism (same seed twice, reused and fresh env), boulder hit = crash, seed ranges, inputs come only from the observation history, numpy/torch network equivalence.\n\nBaselines re-measured on 1,000 fresh flights (seeds 2,000,050,000+, fair boulder layout): pilot v1 72.2% [69.3-74.9], pilot v2 84.0% [81.6-86.1], the old 16-24-4 clone 84.6% [82.2-86.7]. The most common failure is coming to rest just outside the flags (6.6-6.9%), then crashes (4-5%), boulder hits (3.5%), timeouts (0.4-1.3%).\n\nNew warm start: a 2x128 network cloned from pilot v2 with DAgger (4 rounds, 789k steps, 97.7% action agreement) lands 83.5% vs the pilot's 85.9% on the same 1,000 analysis flights: the copy is as good as its source.","kind":"journal"}]